window.RTLBenchLSData.register("assets/d3cd4111d11323e0689cc7adc739317976799336a0089e8c1c80c811d90fd8c2.txt","Module mg_09045 is a simple sequential memory module. \n\nIt has four ports: \n- we (write enable): a single-bit input controlling write operations\n- dataout: a single-bit output providing stored data\n- datain: a single-bit input for data to be written\n- clk: a clock input controlling the module's sequential behavior\n\nInternally, the module has two single-bit memory elements (mem1 and mem2). \n\nWhen the write enable signal is asserted, input data is written to mem1 and then propagated to mem2. \n\nOn every rising clock edge or write enable assertion, the output (dataout) is updated with the current value of mem2.");
